#   🔐 Identity & Access Management (IAM) Architecture

#   Overview

The IAM architecture for Aurum Manufacturing Group (AMG) is designed to provide centralized identity management, secure authentication, and controlled authorization across all cloud and internal resources.

This implementation combines:

* Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) for internal identity

* Azure-native controls for access governance

* Role-based and network-based access enforcement



#   🧱 Identity Architecture Components

1. Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)

* Hosted on: amg-dc01 (Windows Server VM)

* Domain: aurum.local

* Role:

    * Central identity provider for internal resources

    * Authentication for domain-joined machines

    * Group-based access control

Key Functions:

* User authentication (Kerberos / NTLM)

* Organizational Unit (OU) structure for policy control

* Group Policy enforcement

* DNS services for internal name resolution

⸻

2. Organizational Unit (OU) Structure

The AD environment is logically segmented to reflect business roles and enforce administrative boundaries.
 
